            </label>

            <p id="error" role="alert" class="hidden mb-4 text-sm text-red-600">
            </p>

            <button
                id="generate-btn"
                class="w-full px-6 py-3 bg-blue-600 text-white rounded-lg hover:bg-blue-700 font-medium transition"
            >
                Generate Password
            </button>
            <p class="text-xs text-gray-500 mt-2">
                A new password is also created whenever you change a setting.
            </p>
        </section>

        <!-- Generate Multiple -->
        <section class="bg-white p-6 rounded-xl border border-gray-200 mb-6">
            <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold mb-4">Need Multiple Passwords?</h2>
            <p class="text-sm text-gray-600 mb-4">
                Generate 5 passwords at once. Click any password to copy it.
            </p>
            <button
                id="generate-multiple-btn"
                class="px-5 py-2 bg-gray-200 text-gray-800 rounded-lg hover:bg-gray-300 font-medium transition text-sm"
            >
                Generate 5 Passwords
            </button>
            <div id="multiple-output" class="mt-4 space-y-2"></div>
        </section>
    </div>

    <!-- SEO Content -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">About This Password Generator</h2>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This free password generator creates strong, random passwords that
            are practically impossible to guess. It runs entirely in your
            browser, so no password is ever sent to a server. Whether you're
            securing a new email account, a banking login, or a work portal, it
            generates passwords that satisfy the rules of most websites.
        </p>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Most people use weak passwords: pet names, birthdates, or the same
            password across every site. That's how accounts get compromised.
            This tool solves that problem by generating genuinely random
            passwords with your browser's cryptographically secure random number
            generator.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">How to Use</h3>
        <ol class="list-decimal pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                Adjust the password length using the slider (16 characters is a
                good default)
            </li>
            <li>
                Choose which character types to include (uppercase, lowercase,
                numbers, symbols). Every type you select appears at least once.
            </li>
            <li>
                Optionally avoid look-alike characters such as 0, O, 1, l, and I
                if you will type the password by hand
            </li>
            <li>
                Click "Generate Password" for a new one, or just change a
                setting, since the password updates automatically
            </li>
            <li>Click the copy button to copy it to your clipboard</li>
        </ol>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Why Use This Tool?</h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Cryptographically secure:</strong> Uses your browser's built-in
                <code>crypto.getRandomValues</code>, not Math.random().
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Customizable:</strong> Choose length (4–64) and character
                types.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Strength in bits:</strong> The meter shows the entropy of
                the password, not just a guess based on what characters it contains.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Bulk generation:</strong> Generate 5 passwords at once for
                multiple accounts.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Privacy first:</strong> Passwords are created on your device
                and are not stored or sent by this tool.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Free with no limits:</strong> Generate as many passwords as
                you need.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            What Makes a Strong Password?
        </h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Length:</strong> At least 12 characters, ideally 16 or more
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Randomness:</strong> No words, names, dates, or patterns
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Variety:</strong> Mixing uppercase, lowercase, numbers, and
                symbols enlarges the pool of characters
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Uniqueness:</strong> Never reuse a password across sites
            </li>
        </ul>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-3 mb-4">
            Length matters most. Each extra character multiplies the number of
            possible passwords by the size of the character pool. With all four
            character types ({POOL} characters), four more characters make a password
            about {fourMoreCharsFactor} million times harder to guess.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">Common Use Cases</h3>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            1. Creating New Account Passwords
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            For every new account (email, social media, banking, streaming),
            generate a unique password. Store it in a password manager such as
            Bitwarden or 1Password, or in your browser's built-in manager. Never
            reuse passwords across sites.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">2. Replacing Weak Passwords</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            If you're still using "password123" or your dog's name, it's time to
            change. Generate a strong random password and update the account. Do
            this for your most important accounts first (email, banking).
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">3. Wi-Fi Network Passwords</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            A strong Wi-Fi password protects your whole home network. Use 20
            random characters and turn on "Avoid look-alike characters" so it is
            easy to type on other devices. Wi-Fi passphrases must be between 8
            and 63 characters, so keep the length at 63 or below.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">
            4. App Secrets and Database Passwords
        </h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            Developers need strong random values for database passwords and app
            secrets. If the value goes into a URL or a <code>.env</code> file, turn
            off symbols, because characters like <code>#</code>, <code>$</code>,
            and <code>&amp;</code> can need escaping. For cryptographic keys, use
            your platform's key tooling instead of a typed password.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">5. Temporary Access Codes</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            For temporary shared credentials (a guest Wi-Fi password, a shared
            account for a team, a one-time login), use a random password and
            share it through a secure channel.
        </p>

        <h4 class="font-semibold mt-4 mb-2">6. Password Strength Training</h4>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            If you're teaching someone about password security, generate a few
            passwords of different lengths and character combinations and watch
            how the strength in bits changes as you add length.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Strength at Different Lengths
        </h3>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
            This is how the strength meter rates a random password that uses all
            four character types:
        </p>
        <div class="overflow-x-auto">
            <table class="w-full text-sm border border-gray-200 rounded-lg">
                <thead class="bg-gray-50">
                    <tr>
                        <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold border-b"
                            >Length</th
                        >
                        <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold border-b"
                            >Strength (bits)</th
                        >
                        <th class="text-left p-3 font-semibold border-b"
                            >Rating</th
                        >
                    </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody>
                    {
                        strengthRows.map((row) => (
                            <tr>
                                <td class="p-3 border-b">
                                    {row.len} characters
                                </td>
                                <td class="p-3 border-b">about {row.bits}</td>
                                <td class="p-3 border-b">{row.label}</td>
                            </tr>
                        ))
                    }
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-4 mb-4">
            Every extra bit doubles the number of guesses needed. How fast an
            attacker can guess also depends on how the website stores passwords,
            so a unique password for every site matters as much as the length.
        </p>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Password Security Best Practices
        </h3>
        <ul class="list-disc pl-6 text-gray-700 space-y-2">
            <li>
                <strong>Use a password manager:</strong> It's the only practical way
                to have unique passwords for every site.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Never reuse passwords:</strong> If one site is breached, reused
                passwords expose every other account.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Enable two-factor authentication (2FA):</strong> Even a strong
                password isn't enough on its own.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Change passwords after breaches:</strong> If a site you use
                announces a breach, change that password immediately.
            </li>
            <li>
                <strong>Don't share passwords over email or SMS:</strong> Use a password
                manager's sharing feature or an encrypted channel instead.
            </li>
        </ul>

        <h3 class="text-xl font-semibold mt-6 mb-3">
            Frequently Asked Questions
        </h3>
        <div class="space-y-4 mt-3">
            {
                faqs.map((f) => (
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="font-semibold text-gray-900">{f.q}</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 mt-1">{f.a}</p>
                    </div>
                ))
            }
        </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Related Tools -->
    <section class="max-w-3xl mx-auto mt-16">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Related Tools</h2>
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
            <a
                href="/tools/qr-generator/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">QR Code Generator</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Create custom QR codes for any URL.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/unit-converter/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Unit Converter</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Convert length, weight, and temperature.
                </p>
            </a>
            <a
                href="/tools/age-calculator/"
                class="block p-4 bg-white rounded-xl border border-gray-200 hover:shadow-md hover:border-blue-300 transition"
            >
                <h3 class="font-semibold mb-1">Age Calculator</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-gray-600">
                    Find your exact age in years, months, and days.
                </p>
            </a>
        </div>
    </section>

    <script>
        interface Level {
            min: number;
            label: string;
            width: number;
            bar: string;
            text: string;
        }

        const cfg = document.getElementById("calc-config")!;
        const CHAR_SETS: Record<string, string> = JSON.parse(cfg.dataset.sets!);
        const SIMILAR = cfg.dataset.similar!;
        const LEVELS: Level[] = JSON.parse(cfg.dataset.levels!);

        const passwordOutput = document.getElementById(
            "password-output",
        ) as HTMLInputElement;
        const lengthSlider = document.getElementById(
            "length",
        ) as HTMLInputElement;
        const lengthValue = document.getElementById("length-value")!;
        const checks: Record<string, HTMLInputElement> = {
            uppercase: document.getElementById("uppercase") as HTMLInputElement,
            lowercase: document.getElementById("lowercase") as HTMLInputElement,
            numbers: document.getElementById("numbers") as HTMLInputElement,
            symbols: document.getElementById("symbols") as HTMLInputElement,
        };
        const similarCheck = document.getElementById(
            "similar",
        ) as HTMLInputElement;
        const generateBtn = document.getElementById("generate-btn")!;
        const copyBtn = document.getElementById("copy-btn")!;
        const errorBox = document.getElementById("error")!;
        const strengthBar = document.getElementById("strength-bar")!;
        const strengthText = document.getElementById("strength-text")!;
        const generateMultipleBtn = document.getElementById(
            "generate-multiple-btn",
        )!;
        const multipleOutput = document.getElementById("multiple-output")!;

        const COPY_ICON_HTML = copyBtn.innerHTML;

        // Character sets for the checked boxes (minus look-alikes if asked)
        function selectedSets(): string[] {
            const sets: string[] = [];
            for (const name of Object.keys(checks)) {
                if (!checks[name].checked) continue;
                let chars = CHAR_SETS[name];
                if (similarCheck.checked) {
                    chars = [...chars]
                        .filter((c) => !SIMILAR.includes(c))
                        .join("");
                }
                if (chars) sets.push(chars);
            }
            return sets;
        }

        // Uniform random integer in [0, max) from the browser's secure random
        // generator. Values that would cause modulo bias are thrown away.
        function randomInt(max: number): number {
            const limit = Math.floor(0x100000000 / max) * max;
            const buf = new Uint32Array(1);
            let x: number;
            do {
                crypto.getRandomValues(buf);
                x = buf[0];
            } while (x >= limit);
            return x % max;
        }

        // Every character is drawn uniformly from all selected sets. Passwords
        // that are missing a selected type are discarded and drawn again, so the
        // result is uniform over all passwords that contain every selected type.
        function generatePassword(length: number, sets: string[]): string {
            const all = sets.join("");
            const lookups = sets.map((s) => new Set(s));
            let chars: string[] = [];
            for (let attempt = 0; attempt < 100000; attempt++) {
                chars = [];
                for (let i = 0; i < length; i++) {
                    chars.push(all[randomInt(all.length)]);
                }
                if (lookups.every((set) => chars.some((c) => set.has(c))))
                    break;
            }
            return chars.join("");
        }

        // Bits of entropy for a password of `length` characters that must
        // contain at least one character from every set (inclusion-exclusion).
        // Same function as in the page frontmatter.
        function entropyBits(length: number, setSizes: number[]): number {
            const total = setSizes.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0);
            let valid = 0;
            for (let mask = 0; mask < 1 << setSizes.length; mask++) {
                let removed = 0;
                let count = 0;
                for (let i = 0; i < setSizes.length; i++) {
                    if (mask & (1 << i)) {
                        removed += setSizes[i];
                        count++;
                    }
                }
                valid +=
                    (count % 2 ? -1 : 1) * Math.pow(total - removed, length);
            }
            return Math.log2(valid);
        }

        function levelFor(bits: number): Level {
            let level = LEVELS[0];
            for (const l of LEVELS) if (bits >= l.min) level = l;
            return level;
        }

        function updateStrength(length: number, sets: string[]) {
            const bits = entropyBits(
                length,
                sets.map((s) => s.length),
            );
            const level = levelFor(bits);
            strengthBar.style.width = level.width + "%";
            strengthBar.className =
                "h-full transition-all duration-300 " + level.bar;
            strengthText.textContent = `${level.label} (about ${Math.round(bits)} bits)`;
            strengthText.className = "text-sm font-medium " + level.text;
        }

        function showError(message: string) {
            errorBox.textContent = message;
            errorBox.classList.remove("hidden");
        }

        function generate() {
            const sets = selectedSets();
            if (sets.length === 0) {
                showError("Please select at least one character type.");
                return;
            }
            errorBox.classList.add("hidden");
            const length = Math.max(
                parseInt(lengthSlider.value, 10),
                sets.length,
            );
            const password = generatePassword(length, sets);
            passwordOutput.value = password;
            updateStrength(length, sets);
        }

        async function copyText(text: string): Promise<boolean> {
            try {
                await navigator.clipboard.writeText(text);
                return true;
            } catch {
                // Fallback for browsers that block the clipboard API
                try {
                    const ta = document.createElement("textarea");
                    ta.value = text;
                    ta.style.position = "fixed";
                    ta.style.opacity = "0";
                    document.body.appendChild(ta);
                    ta.select();
                    const ok = document.execCommand("copy");
                    document.body.removeChild(ta);
                    return ok;
                } catch {
                    return false;
                }
            }
        }

        // Generate again whenever a setting changes
        lengthSlider.addEventListener("input", () => {
            lengthValue.textContent = lengthSlider.value;
            generate();
        });
        Object.values(checks).forEach((el) =>
            el.addEventListener("change", generate),
        );
        similarCheck.addEventListener("change", generate);
        generateBtn.addEventListener("click", generate);

        let copyTimer: number | undefined;
        copyBtn.addEventListener("click", async () => {
            if (!passwordOutput.value) return;
            const ok = await copyText(passwordOutput.value);
            copyBtn.innerHTML = `<span class="text-sm">${ok ? "Copied!" : "Copy failed"}</span>`;
            window.clearTimeout(copyTimer);
            copyTimer = window.setTimeout(
                () => (copyBtn.innerHTML = COPY_ICON_HTML),
                1500,
            );
        });

        generateMultipleBtn.addEventListener("click", () => {
            const sets = selectedSets();
            if (sets.length === 0) {
                showError("Please select at least one character type.");
                return;
            }
            errorBox.classList.add("hidden");
            const length = Math.max(
                parseInt(lengthSlider.value, 10),
                sets.length,
            );
            multipleOutput.innerHTML = "";
            for (let i = 0; i < 5; i++) {
                const password = generatePassword(length, sets);
                const row = document.createElement("button");
                row.className =
                    "w-full text-left p-3 bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-lg font-mono text-sm hover:bg-blue-50 hover:border-blue-300 transition";
                row.textContent = password;
                let timer: number | undefined;
                row.addEventListener("click", async () => {
                    const ok = await copyText(password);
                    row.textContent = ok ? "✓ Copied!" : "✗ Copy failed";
                    window.clearTimeout(timer);
                    // Restore from the saved password, never from the button text
                    timer = window.setTimeout(
                        () => (row.textContent = password),
                        1500,
                    );
                });
                multipleOutput.appendChild(row);
            }
        });

        // Generate a first password on load
        generate();
    </script>

    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify(webAppSchema)}
    />
    <script
        type="application/ld+json"
        set:html={JSON.stringify(breadcrumbSchema)}
    />
    <script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(faqSchema)} />
</Layout>
